# Changelog management

Index: [docs/changelog](../../docs/changelog/README.md)

Changelogs are **user-facing release notes**, not a commit log. One **in-progress file per minor line** (`1.2.x`), frozen to the **exact patch** on ship (`1.2.165`), not per push.

**The changelog does not decide the version or codename.** The release admin picks the exact version at release time (CI bump / chosen tag); the codename comes from `kReleaseCodename` in [`app_version.dart`](../../apps/forja/lib/shared/services/app_version.dart). The changelog only carries the **bullets** — its `# 1.2.x — …` title is a human placeholder that CI ignores for numbering and naming.

## Golden rules

1. **One draft per minor arc** — while shipping `1.2.x` patches, all pushed work updates `docs/changelog/1.2.x-[draft].md` until the next tag.
2. **Same turn as code** — when a change is user-visible, update the active changelog in the **same turn** as code and [feature docs](../../docs/features/README.md).
3. **Final truth only** — edit or remove bullets when a later push corrects or reverts earlier work. No history of wrong attempts.
4. **Short and readable** — complete for users, synthesized. No RFC/issue IDs, file paths, or implementation detail.
5. **Version & codename are external** — admin sets the version at release; codename lives in `kReleaseCodename`. Never treat the changelog title as the source for either.

## Which file is active?

| App minor (`pubspec` / `kReleaseCodename`) | Draft file |
|--------------------------------------------|------------|
| `1.2.x` (today) | `docs/changelog/1.2.x-[draft].md` |
| `1.3.x` (future) | `docs/changelog/1.3.x-[draft].md` |

Minor bumps (`1.2` → `1.3`) start a **new** `X.Y.x-[draft].md`. Patch backlog files (`docs/backlog/1.0.1-…`) schedule RFC/issue work — **changelog draft name follows app minor + `x`**, not backlog patch filenames.

## File lifecycle

```
pushing     →  docs/changelog/1.2.x-[draft].md     (accumulate bullets since last tag)
admin ships  →  admin picks version (e.g. 1.2.165); CI builds the release body from the draft
freeze      →  docs/changelog/done/1.2.165-[released].md   (title = shipped version)
next pushes →  docs/changelog/1.2.x-[draft].md     (fresh empty sections; **Since release:** 1.2.165)
minor 1.3.0 →  update kReleaseCodename + new docs/changelog/1.3.x-[draft].md
```

On release (admin picks version, then git tag `vX.Y.Z`):

1. **You (human):** Prune bullets for work that did not ship; ensure wording matches the tagged build — do this **before** running the release workflow, since the freeze snapshots the draft into the tagged commit.
2. **CI (automatic):** The `Release Forja` workflow runs [`scripts/changelog_freeze.sh <version>`](../../scripts/changelog_freeze.sh) in the version-bump step, **before** it commits and tags. That script:
   - moves the draft to `docs/changelog/done/X.Y.Z-[released].md` (title `# X.Y.Z — <codename>`, body `**Status:** released`),
   - refreshes the [changelog README](../../docs/changelog/README.md) **Active** row + **Released** table,
   - starts a fresh empty `docs/changelog/X.Y.x-[draft].md` with `**Since release:**` pointing at the version just shipped — **no group headings** until the first bullet (see [template](#template-draft-file)).
   These changes are part of the `chore: release vX.Y.Z` commit, so the tag contains the frozen released file and the fresh draft.

The freeze is **idempotent** — if `done/X.Y.Z-[released].md` already exists or the draft is missing, it is a no-op (so re-runs and the "Existing tag" release mode are safe). Only run `changelog_freeze.sh` by hand when a release was tagged without it (older workflow) and you need to backfill.

When bumping to a **new minor** (`1.2` → `1.3`): update `kReleaseCodename` in `app_version.dart` to the new minor's codename ([runway](../../docs/backlog/README.md#codename-runway)) and start `1.3.x-[draft].md`. CI reads the codename from `app_version.dart`, so this keeps the release title correct without editing the changelog title.

## CI integration (automatic release body)

The `publish_release` job in [`.github/workflows/release.yml`](../../.github/workflows/release.yml) checks out the tagged commit and runs [`scripts/changelog_release_notes.sh <version>`](../../scripts/changelog_release_notes.sh), where `<version>` is the exact version the **admin** resolved for the release. The script:

- resolves the codename from `kReleaseCodename` in `app_version.dart` (not the changelog title),
- builds the title as `# <version> — <codename>` (e.g. `# 1.2.165 — Dabaghin`),
- pulls bullets from the frozen `docs/changelog/done/<version>-[released].md` (written by `changelog_freeze.sh` earlier in the same run), falling back to `docs/changelog/{major}.{minor}.x-[draft].md` if the freeze did not run,
- drops empty thematic groups + editor scaffolding,
- feeds the result as the GitHub Release **body**.

That body is what `AppUpdaterService` fetches and the in-app update dialog shows — so **the draft must be clean and correct at tag time**. If no draft exists (or it has no group with bullets), CI falls back to `generate_release_notes` (raw commit list). Keep bullets user-facing so the update dialog stays readable.

## When to add a bullet

| Change | Changelog? |
|--------|------------|
| New user-visible feature, screen, setting, provider | ✅ |
| Bug fix users would notice | ✅ |
| UX copy, layout, or behavior change users see | ✅ |
| Internal refactor, tests, CI, docs-only (no user impact) | ❌ |
| Workaround shipped — describe user impact honestly | ✅ |

Derive bullets from **what changed for the user**, not backlog `B*-S*` IDs.

## Writing style

- **Audience:** someone updating the app.
- **One line per item** — start with an [action prefix](#action-prefixes), then the outcome.
- **Thematic groups** — use the [Forja groups](#thematic-groups-forja) below; **add a `### Group` heading only when that group has bullets** — never leave empty group headers in the draft (CI and the update dialog omit them automatically).
- **Group** related items into one bullet when they share one user story.
- **No** task IDs, issue numbers, crate names, or internal refactors unless user-visible.

## Action prefixes

Every bullet **must** start with one of these — **bold** Title case + colon:

| Prefix | Use when |
|--------|----------|
| `**Add:**` | New capability, screen, setting, provider, or option |
| `**Change:**` | Existing behavior or layout updated (not a bug) |
| `**Fix:**` | Bug or broken UX users would notice |
| `**Remove:**` | Something taken away |

Format: `- **Fix:** Live match embeds on Windows no longer open white.`

Do **not** invent extra verbs (`Improve:`, `Update:`, `Refactor:`). Map to the four above (`Improve` → `Change` or `Fix`).

## Thematic groups (Forja)

Six groups — pick **one** per bullet. Do not add sub-groups or extra headings.

| Group | Use for | Examples |
|-------|---------|----------|
| **Features** | New screens, tabs, workflows, integrations users discover | Anime hub, Cmd+F search, settings category hub, new Jellyfin slice |
| **Player** | Playback, controls, subtitles, PiP, speed, skip intro, next episode, external player | Flat player menus, seek preview, auto next episode |
| **UI** | Shell, home, details layout, navigation, cards, hero, design polish, About/labels | Home hero layout, details metadata, settings layout (not provider logic) |
| **Sources** | Stream providers, torrent resolve, embeds, scrapers, debrid, auto-resolve, cache | New VidSrc provider, dead-cache re-resolve, KissKh extract reliability |
| **Live & IPTV** | Live Matches, Xtream, M3U, embed player for sports/IPTV | Stream picker, iframe embed fix, IPTV channel grid |
| **TV** | Android TV, leanback launcher, D-pad focus, TV-only shell | ATV tab focus, WebView GLES workaround on TV |

**Engine / Rust:** no separate group. If users would notice, phrase as an outcome under **Sources** (faster or more reliable resolve), **Player** (smoother open), or **Features** (new capability). Never “refactored crate X”.

**Platform-specific:** put the bullet under the feature group (e.g. Windows live embed → **Live & IPTV**), not a “Windows” section.

### Template (draft file)

Start with no group headings. When you add the first bullet for a group, add its `###` heading above it:

```markdown
### UI
- **Change:** …

### Sources
- **Add:** …
- **Fix:** …
```

Do **not** pre-fill all six groups with empty `###` headings.

### Good

```markdown
### Live & IPTV
- **Fix:** Live match embeds on Windows no longer open as a white transparent surface.

### Sources
- **Fix:** Auto-resolve skips dead cached links and tries the next server.
- **Add:** VidSrc.sbs as a stream provider.
```

### Bad

```markdown
### Fixed
- Issue 053: WebView2 transparent background workaround.

### Engine
- Renamed resolver-engine crate.

### UI
- Settings About cleaned up.   ← missing **Add:** / **Change:** / **Fix:** / **Remove:**
- Fix: missing bold on the prefix.
```

## Correcting earlier entries (mandatory)

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Fix changes user-visible outcome | **Edit** the existing bullet |
| Feature dropped or reverted before ship | **Remove** the bullet |
| Two pushes same fix | **One** bullet |
| Push A added X, push B removed X | **No bullet** for X |

